§11 NEW FINDING F-55: THREE DEVTOOLS SCREENSHOTS ARE BYTE-IDENTICAL
  reevidence-06-devtools-screenshot-dedup.txt: rc-create-node / rc-error-report / rc-inspect-scene
  = 5254 B, sha16 80cdb10343a2ac68 for all three (480x360). They were re-captured by this pass and
  came out identical again, so this is reproducible, not a one-off write collision.
  Decoded pixel content (zlib + unfilter, E:/qoder-pngflat.cjs): NOT a blank frame — 6 distinct
  sampled colors, clear color 1e283c, scene pixel 0b331d; automation has 7 colors with a lit centre.
  Cause is upstream of the capture: rc-error-report and rc-inspect-scene declare the same
  expectedGraph (Main Camera, Main Light, DemoCube) and the same single visual validator
  ["visible-frame"]; rc-create-node only adds a hidden AgentGenerated node, so its frame matches.
  Consequence: the Screenshot Current binding has teeth (a replaced or truncated frame fails), but
  for visible-frame-only examples the frame cannot distinguish one example from another. The fix is
  a spec decision (a per-example visual validator, e.g. node-count or a transform-diff region), not
  a tooling change -> F-55, deliberately not made by the audit agent.

§12 COMMIT BOUNDARY DECISION (why the regenerated evidence is not in my commit)
  The gate compares specFingerprint(example.json) against the evidence record. 61 dirty
  examples/*/example.json are parallel-session edits that my pass did not write, and the fresh
  evidence was hashed against THOSE specs. Committing docs/evidence/** without examples/** would
  produce a commit that fails S11-STALE-EVIDENCE on a clean checkout; committing examples/** would
  land another session's in-flight work under an audit commit message. Both are worse than the
  chosen boundary:
    committed by this audit: tools/verify/v11-spec-common.cjs, tools/examples/spec-compliance-audit.cjs,
                             docs/audits/global-quality-audit-2026-09-19/** (ledger + raw logs, force-added)
    left in the working tree for the owner's V1.1 commit: docs/evidence/** (regenerated 12:05-12:13Z),
                             examples/** (their in-flight specs; this pass wrote none of them)
  The two new tools are INERT at HEAD: nothing tracked at HEAD requires them (git grep found no
  consumer of v11-spec-common in HEAD; HEAD's smoke-29 does not reference spec-compliance-audit),
  so committing them cannot make the committed tree red. That was checked before staging.

